Issue #19 is not finished: the fix is committed and queued to land on main, but no build can run, so it isn't merged, tested or released yet.

- **The fix:** commit 32297cb moves `tacplus.lock` from tacplus 2.6.1 to 2.6.8, at its build image's digest. That image compiles with go1.27.4, which fixes GO-2026-6859. The 2.6 floor is unchanged, and `STATE.md` is updated.
- **Why it didn't land:** the previous red verdict was not a failed test. Both build jobs so far (pipelines 3053721343 and 3054110148) stopped after 3 hours with no result, because no build runner is picking up jobs. That is tacplus-dev/looper#113, caused by tacplus-dev/cluster#18, which is open and waiting on a decision from Jody. Since 05:00Z every land in the looper repository has failed the same way.
- **What I did:** I queued the land with the manager once more at 14:52Z. The manager will still merge it after this run if a build goes green. I didn't start another separate build, since it would only add another 3-hour job to the stalled pool. I posted a status comment on #19 and wrote `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cluster#18` to the run's outcome file.
- **Not yet checked:** `just gates` on the new pin, and `govulncheck -mode=binary` on the built `bin/blobstore`. Both need a build job that actually runs.
- **Still to do:** once the land is green, the next run tags and pushes `v0.1.3` at the landed commit. It can be cut from main because main has only `HISTORY.md` commits since `v0.1.2`. Then it posts the outcome comment and closes #19. There are no `release/*` branches, so nothing needs backporting.

The change touches no service handlers, so the trace-propagation rule doesn't apply.
